<title>BRAZIL: Brazil allows Light to raise rates - paper.</title>
<headline>Brazil allows Light to raise rates - paper.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Brazilian government authorised Rio de Janeiro-based power distributor Light to raise its electricity rates by 8.038 percent, O Globo newspaper said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The rate hike meets the terms of a concession contract signed when the firm was privatized in May. Under the contract, Light would be allowed to raise rates annually according to an inflation-based formula. The firm's last adjustment was in November 1995.</p>
<p>Light is controlled by a group of local and foreign companies, comprising France's EDF and U.S. firms Houston Industries and AES Corp, Brazilian private steel mill CSN and BNDES Participacoes (BNDESPar), the investment arm of the National Development Bank (BNDES.</p>
<p>-- Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo Newsroom, 55-11-2485412</p>
